  "id": "articulatory-suppression",
  "term": "articulatory suppression",
  "definition": "Articulatory suppression is a research method used to create verbal interference by having a person repeat syllables or words, aloud or subvocally, while doing another task. It is intended to block or reduce the use of inner speech or other verbal strategies, especially when studying phonological or language-related processing.",
